From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=81ngel=20Ren=C3=A9?=
 <17342133+angelrenefm@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:33:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: s5p-mfc: don't lose the FRAME_DONE that stop_streaming
 waits for
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When a queue is stopped while the context's frame is being decoded,
stop_streaming() sets MFCINST_ABORT and waits for FRAME_DONE. The
interrupt handler of that frame wakes the context up, releases the
hardware and calls try_run, which picks the same context again because
its work bit is still set. try_run clears the context's interrupt flags
before finding nothing to run in MFCINST_ABORT, so the waiter finds no
FRAME_DONE and the STREAMOFF stalls for the full two second timeout,
logging "Interrupt (ctx->int_type:0, command:13) timed out".

Clear the work bit together with setting MFCINST_ABORT. On the Pixel 7
every seek in GStreamer took two seconds and logged that timeout; with
this, three runs of two seeks each logged none and resumed at once.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ángel René <17342133+angelrenefm@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_dec.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_dec.c b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_dec.c
index e151b5a39..3d10dcccf 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_dec.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_dec.c
@@ -1125,6 +1125,14 @@ static void s5p_mfc_stop_streaming(struct vb2_queue *q)
 		ctx->state ==  MFCINST_RUNNING) &&
 		dev->curr_ctx == ctx->num && dev->hw_lock) {
 		ctx->state = MFCINST_ABORT;
+		/*
+		 * Take the context off the run queue. Otherwise the interrupt
+		 * handler of the frame being decoded picks it again in
+		 * try_run, which clears the context's interrupt flags before
+		 * finding nothing to run in MFCINST_ABORT, and the wait below
+		 * misses that FRAME_DONE and times out.
+		 */
+		clear_work_bit(ctx);
 		spin_unlock_irqrestore(&dev->irqlock, flags);
 		s5p_mfc_wait_for_done_ctx(ctx,
 					S5P_MFC_R2H_CMD_FRAME_DONE_RET, 0);
